{"id": "EUVD-2026-59664", "enisaUuid": "e5fb8c15-bce1-30de-964c-1e24bf10a76d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing: Check return value of __register_event() in trace_module_add_events()\n\ntrace_module_add_events() ignores the return value of __register_event()\nand unconditionally calls __add_event_to_tracers() for each event.\n\nIf __register_event() fails (for example, if event_init() fails), the\ntrace_event_call is not added to ftrace_events list, but\n__add_event_to_tracers() still creates a trace_event_file pointing to it.\nIf module loading subsequently fails and module memory is freed, tracing\nstate retains a stale trace_event_call pointer in trace_event_file,\nleading to a use-after-free when tracefs or tracing subsystem operations\nare later executed.\n\nFix this by checking the return value of __register_event() and only\ncalling __add_event_to_tracers() if event registration succeeded.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T12:27:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:05:47", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3bf965a2827c44f03294107703e7ba53fbd0a69a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d6d79744f01eacaf3d5522f4fcd59939581abfd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/54b7a358f6399c1242d2fb7f4f96085af34baa5e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d61ee2a27dfd5eb43ddc18af40168f5b9eb1cea5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22f954f7a8afe975e85517aff41b35defe05144b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cbb5ed3be9cae70e1c12b1991009b4e12bf4a4ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/000765dcdc3edf128990762790543adc4b868f6c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac8719969e6c3c54e939834df812bc41f25453cf"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74471", "GHSA-437h-q69x-6qrx"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "12848a49-aad7-3732-86ec-3f85233eed58", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae63b31e4d0e2ec09c569306ea46f664508ef717 <9d6d79744f01eacaf3d5522f4fcd59939581abfd"}, {"id": "143dc7f3-a986-31b1-9416-b3dc80d7695b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae63b31e4d0e2ec09c569306ea46f664508ef717 <ac8719969e6c3c54e939834df812bc41f25453cf"}, {"id": "336d6dbf-c437-3951-b06d-6757df2b0aee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.8"}, {"id": "42cd5913-4447-3b49-9ea0-58a07d872047", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4b60d130-e885-38c8-a6d6-519ebda758e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae63b31e4d0e2ec09c569306ea46f664508ef717 <54b7a358f6399c1242d2fb7f4f96085af34baa5e"}, {"id": "7015e8ad-348c-3801-94c0-9d38bb23d53c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.183"}, {"id": "752f1198-e2e8-337e-b9f5-41887ca052a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.44"}, {"id": "7aff29e0-f3dc-3067-9ce1-2743283aa94b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.265"}, {"id": "7ebc8bb8-bb41-3b67-9098-3230c0a92936", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.10"}, {"id": "88d2f7b9-1299-30cf-a9b8-08e8361e28f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.216"}, {"id": "9281c67c-f0cd-393a-b5d6-adb799933591", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "94216a68-71f6-345e-bc33-e76a015bf8f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae63b31e4d0e2ec09c569306ea46f664508ef717 <cbb5ed3be9cae70e1c12b1991009b4e12bf4a4ca"}, {"id": "a22d2ba9-3496-3654-9c73-8140cd748a2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version":